  "title": "Qt: Software Update: Windows: Respect thread affinity of QTimer",
  "description": "A QTimer can only be started or stopped from its owning thread,\nso that the timeout signal is emitted from the proper thread.\nWinSparkle can call SoftwareUpdate::softwareUpdateEngaged() from\nanother thread.\n\nUse QMetaObject::invokeMethod with a QueuedConnection to ensure\nthat all the behavior is done in the proper thread.\n\nFix #21456",
